Metal tensor-API flash attention (Apple M5 and newer): the tensor kernel required a KV length that is a multiple of 64
and otherwise fell back to the half8x8 simdgroup kernel at about half the throughput, which DiTs with text tokens
appended to image tokens (Z-Image: 4096 + 32) always hit. The partial last KV chunk is now copied into the existing
pad buffer by kernel_flash_attn_ext_pad and read from there; columns past the KV length are set to -MAXHALF after
softcap, as in the half8x8 kernel. GPUs without the tensor API and KV lengths that are a multiple of 64 run the same pipelines as before.

